 Preserve original independent outputs before informed synthesis. Give reviewers outcome, unchanged charter, exact target artifacts and actual environment, not the author's desired findings or answer key. Disclose unavoidable historical judgments inside existing specifications. Use actual role reports to support a team-run claim; assigning labels to one self-review does not establish independently executed teams. An informed review of this explicit proposal does not test whether the method would have independently discovered the earlier need.
 
-**Plugin contextual application.** Candidate plugin profiles and lifecycle constraints belong to canonical 01–05/07. Compare source/content contributions, external executors, analysis/report and admitted UI behavior against their own effects; Obsidian remains an example. Borrow a narrow versioned interface or lifecycle lesson only with its assumptions. Keep signatures, process placement, containment and current authorization separate. Do not infer that a general plugin registry exists from executor MCP support or that a successful document review selects the first implementation.
